  {
   "id": "HNZOnWPl-CUJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2014-10-17T16:14:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Properly Running Chains in Parallel",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Yes, the key is having different chain_id.  This advances\r<br>the random number generator a very big step (more than you&#39;d\r<br>have time to genrate), thus making the draws in the different chains\r<br>come from different slices of the pseudo-random number sequence\r<br>determined by the seed.  \r<br>\r<br>This works the same way in the other interfaces, too.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Oct 17, 2014, at 12:09 PM, Markian Pahuta &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mark....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>\r<br>&gt; Hi\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I just want to make sure that I will be running 3 independent chains with the following code (I&#39;m using Linux). Specifically, am I defining rng_seed OK?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; library(parallel)\r<br>&gt; library(rstan)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; setwd(&#39;~/ions/&#39;)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; load(&#39;Co_data_oct16.dat&#39;)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; foo &lt;- stan(file = &#39;oct16.stan&#39;, data = datalist, chains=0)\r<br>&gt; rng_seed &lt;-12345\r<br>&gt; sflist &lt;- mclapply(\r<br>&gt;           1:3, \r<br>&gt;           mc.cores = 3, \r<br>&gt;            function(i) stan(fit = foo, \r<br>&gt;                             data = datalist, \r<br>&gt;                             iter=5000,\r<br>&gt;                             thin=5,\r<br>&gt;                             seed = rng_seed, \r<br>&gt;                             chains = 1, \r<br>&gt;                             chain_id = i, \r<br>&gt;                             refresh = -1))\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; modfit &lt;- sflist2stanfit(sflist)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; thanks\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Mark\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
